<title>INDIA: India RBI resumes dollar buying at 35.70 rupees.</title>
<headline>India RBI resumes dollar buying at 35.70 rupees.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) bought dollars at 35.700/705 levels in Wednesday afternoon trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;He just bought at 35.705,&quot; said a foreign bank dealer.</p>
<p>RBI has been regularly buying dollars in recent weeks, preventing the rupee's rise above the 35.70-mark.</p>
<p>The rupee was quoted at 35.700/707 rupees in latest deals.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
